                 \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$].$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The period of the function is\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-5}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=sin⁡x.$\n\n![](images/96/96bd60d23237f836b77a26c5c0461a5c2a474554f0a14266b53fc5e7d999f1b7.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n* The domain of the function is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n* The minimum value is $-1,$ and the maximum value is $1.$ Therefore, the range is $[-1,1].$\n\n* The period of $sin⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc2ce46-b2a6-56de-8ead-93675bda43d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236005} {:answer/id #uuid "86f59763-455d-5124-95ad-635362b1efd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236659} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3a