 "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236162} {:answer/id #uuid "431b8b2c-60f9-50ed-a73e-335785cc18ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236250} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c131e4-70f4-5b57-9ffb-981148d71879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236948} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d7012c-5356-5c36-b422-e156f9cbdec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2c131e4-70f4-5b57-9ffb-981148d71879" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236948} :answer-field/id #uuid "49b37897-7ab2-5034-96e3-b9f2f4798c3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237534}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4afb86c8-970f-594e-bb88-36f6e2c3e725" :question/math-academy-id "q-103233" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The zeros of the function are $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,1)$\n- The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The zeros occur at $x=\\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pm \\frac{3\\pi }{2},…,$ which can be written as $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=0,$ the function has the value $y=cos⁡0=1.$ Therefore, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,1).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292696 :question/answe