is false. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338799 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0332655e-d2f9-5b01-81c8-6bf921b57cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336060} {:answer/id #uuid "34ca9964-2c59-5dd8-857d-7da898ef6dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336529} {:answer/id #uuid "72087625-2679-52b3-b69e-0ad275f1585c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337053} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3d294d-ab01-5b32-a809-1d323af163c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337713} {:answer/id #uuid "de41d8d4-ce87-53e0-9f71-2a6926fe0ba5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72087625-2679-52b3-b69e-0ad275f1585c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337053} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd6a7dab-a086-5096-985b-55b73b3634c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338726}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5773d37-2017-53ae-a0d1-64c772d0dcaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-70666" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has maximum values at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$\n- The function is zero at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has a maximum at $x=0,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=2n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. At $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338800 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19e1f0f6-cdd9-56b4-a97c-62ec04052296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336270} {:answer/id #uuid "55a003f4-6613-50bf-8dc5-00b12c062d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336819} {:answer/id #uuid "65829911-343f-5184-8bfd-a51d9cbc6ccc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336938} {:answer/id #uuid "857b0866-840f-5787-8f25-33109f144e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337235} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb894de-3d54-53ec-a8ac-6af5ea4bb2f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19e1f0f6-cdd9-56b4-a97c-62ec04052296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336270} :answer-field/id #uuid "d460533e-ecf9-527d-9c80-5091452ea8df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338651}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24b90149-221d-555e-91aa-b1d1cb7cb1c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-70667" :question/problem "Which of the following statements regarding the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ are true?\n\nI. The graph intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1$\n\nII. The function has a minimum value at $x=-\\pi .$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/88/88378ece5b1721cdc533d07d69c004901539c7f8fda9a5a3e5c5648ed32905c5.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The $y$-intercepts of the function is $y=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function at $x=-\\pi $ has a minimum value.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$, the maximum value is $1$, and so the range is $[-1,1].$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176048 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175694 :question/id #uuid "a8cc8b8f-463b-5734-a33d-e915159cba32" :question/math-academy-id "e-11003" :question/problem "If $\\cos x =- \\dfrac {1}{3},$ find the value of $2\\cos( x + 4\\pi)+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y = \\cos x$ is $2\\pi.$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\cos{x} = \\cos{(x+2n\\pi)} .\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=2$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x & =cos⁡(x+2\\cdot 2\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cos⁡(x+4\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\cos{x} =- \\dfrac {1}{3},$ then $\\cos{(x+4\\pi)} = - \\dfrac {1}{3}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2cos⁡(x+4\\pi )+3 & =2(-\\frac{1}{3})+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}+3 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1c25c3a0-083a-55d5-b688-7347bfafaa9e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049353 :topic/math-academy-id 2148 :topic/title "Periodic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88f28e6a-97ea-5e36-bf74-369bcac3c4bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175415} {:answer/id #uuid "9e88cd39-4060-5bbd-a35c-9862da2c6a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175416} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd05264-d89f-5106-8257-5d4ac26b1665" :answer/t