" :question/problem "If $\\cos x =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$, then $\\cos (x + 10π) =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fe07cef-135a-5aee-b857-d8421aa48542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235900} {:answer/id #uuid "13614331-5578-515d-8943-8af84bd83334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi -\\frac{3}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235929} {:answer/id #uuid "89e2a1f7-298a-5958-86d7-db27000a04bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}+2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236680} {:answer/id #uuid "bb07dd52-f518-54f6-8f86-fe701c1ada44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi -\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237014} {:answer/id #uuid "e2f1e392-4f36-5478-9ad8-f088d40891d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2f1e392-4f36-5478-9ad8-f088d40891d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237242} :answer-field/id #uuid "9baaf465-f7d4-5147-8968-33136247a92f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237647}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d276077-f8d6-5c9d-ba5b-27234154bb37" :question/math-academy-id "q-103242" :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=-\\frac{5}{8},$ then $cos⁡(x+12\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for an integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=6$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2\\cdot 6\\cdot \\pi )=cos⁡(x+12\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=-\\frac{5}{8},$ then $cos⁡(x+12\\pi )=-\\frac{5}{8}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237985 :ques