answer/id #uuid "a0e7978b-65fb-572d-9e69-fb0ed478e885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337487} {:answer/id #uuid "c8d773d6-1137-500e-9144-d700b2fde742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337808} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c26a46-9433-52e8-869e-79e45ee386aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337927} {:answer/id #uuid "de73e983-b2d8-5bee-8dbc-77304e29d367" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337970} {:answer/id #uuid "e38b4e0e-34f4-5b2c-bf38-151d565a04ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}+10\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338018}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0e7978b-65fb-572d-9e69-fb0ed478e885" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337487} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd7d23c2-12b8-516e-b527-7ded32873395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338666}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c70c4bc0-3980-5503-a6a2-bd4be92dae51" :question/math-academy-id "q-70671" :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}$ for some $x$, then $cos⁡(x-10\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x-10\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=\\frac{1}{2},$ then $cos⁡(x-10\\pi )=\\frac{1}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338803 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c81bece-db23-58d8-bb4c-a4ec954ab3a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336150} {:answer/id #uuid "11454d75-ea49-5be3-97d8-331be00c105f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+2\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336195} {:answer/id #uuid "180fc6bd-ead7-54b4-bbdc-eccc651de809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+16\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336255} {:answer/id #uuid "aa67f4b1-dac9-5c08-9fd9-fcd2b26eb1d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337568} {:answer/id #uuid "e2a95a14-3cbb-500b-8ddd-ebf38336d4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}+16\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c81bece-db23-58d8-bb4c-a4ec954ab3a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336150} :answer-field/id #uuid "c49b55a2-50e7-5337-b7ac-4eaf751dacaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338629}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6abcc021-8010-5554-b152-291688c68aef" :question/math-academy-id "q-70672" :question/problem "If $cos⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for some $x$, then $cos⁡(x+16\\pi )=$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=cos⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡x=cos⁡(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=8$ into the right-hand-side gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cos⁡x=cos⁡(x+16\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cos⁡x=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ then $cos⁡(x+16\\pi )=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Cosine Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175695 :question/id #uuid "2f4571af-99cf-5a4a-9998-fb6a0f7d6be9" :question/math-academy-id "e-11004" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The zeros of the function are at $x = \\pi n.$\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x = 2\\pi n.$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in [-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The zeros occur at $x=0, \\pm \\pi, \\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has an asymptote at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x = \\dfrac \\pi 2 + \\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty, \\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049155 :topic/math-academy-id 1493 :topic/title "Graphing Tangent and Cotangent"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176452 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dadb8ed-d007-53f9-b484-29cf8f9a60a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290758} {:answer/id #uuid "66c9cd18-91c7-5e08-b042-2a46c28131c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291069} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad75161-3e9a-5223-a9dd-e94c64654137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291218} {:answer/id #uuid "8dc52d0d-4f4a-5cc2-b0ef-5fca8c28e540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291239} {:answer/id #uuid "f8178445-42e3-5a5f-bf77-90e72387e35e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dadb8ed-d007-53f9-b484-29cf8f9a60a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290758} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8e4e113-a95b-5d5a-b2fa-1d2198192c93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292347}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ac898e3a-bbc1-536e-8415-2d3fbc798e28" :question/math-academy-id "q-27638" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n- The function returns only positive values on the intervals $(\\pi n,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n)\\,.$\n- The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/32/326418398ce1a33f03a21f3bdb58107856f4ccb72241429f1604486281e60822.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function returns only positive values on the interval $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the function is positive on $(n\\pi ,\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi )\\,.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f15d390-a048-5eb4-a046-310acd367f7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174859} {:answer/id #uuid "e88f93a9-f633-5861-9b67-f9258797c25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174860} {:answer/id #uuid "448fad8e-383b-5721-928b-2f98064401f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174861} {:answer/id #uuid "47ec71cf-a994-50c7-8ca5-ac57ea5d0ea0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174862} {:answer/id #uuid "5ea9d9e5-e787-5660-bc70-c91a945b6f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174863}] :answer-field/id #uuid "02d7e3e2-9588-558a-8337-8446e8238d6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174858}] :question/id #uuid "95d49fd8-cd30-53eb-a4a3-b8a8c0494e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-27660" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\tan x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The function has asymptotes at $x = \\frac{π}{2} + πn$.\n2. The range of the function is $y ∈ (-\\frac{π}{2}, \\frac{π}{2})$.\n3. The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x = nπ$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237987 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c2f2bf1-9489-53d0-aef7-7228b981bac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235998} {:answer/id #uuid "1ff2b5ac-aa6d-5187-84fd-8accf825947a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236023} {:answer/id #uuid "4126e729-233b-53a1-875e-c58b84df84ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236232} {:answer/id #uuid "75f6292f-0f0c-5b71-9614-126a4b2d68e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236556} {:answer/id #uuid "83034a3e-d469-513a-b703-047d7a3470a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c2f2bf1-9489-53d0-aef7-7228b981bac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235998} :answer-field/id #uuid "92061e84-03fe-54ba-9008-b9fd45a3987b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237633}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2215b590-8140-5323-92bf-8ae24e1b7bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-103289" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nI. The domain of the function is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $\n\nII. The function has zeros at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/73/732955302ca49a41f6c43cf242d7c869e630e88d804c4b56a5beb3b081f2d230.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function is defined everywhere, except where $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm \\pi ,\\pm 2\\pi ,…,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d059bf-52c4-58a9-9b0a-80f98273a3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236136} {:answer/id #uuid "60ffe8f6-7519-5c83-8e3b-7933d314d384" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236435} {:answer/id #uuid "760810ba-4dba-5546-b9e0-25979b61215c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236557} {:answer/id #uuid "c375d3e0-e998-53aa-9b1a-df787d700c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237052} {:answer/id #uuid "de60a5ae-237a-5bdb-ad3c-19e44d3dcfba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "760810ba-4dba-5546-b9e0-25979b61215c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236557} :answer-field/id #uuid "137c3137-fea5-56a8-8a43-b7a5f0e8b08b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237462}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6f5925ee-40c3-50af-9950-ecf1ea188724" :question/math-academy-id "q-103295" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- The vertical asymptotes of the function are $x=2n\\pi $\n- Its graph passes through the point $(0,0)$\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2d0606829588b01f6cba2fa4785b201c47a6d9ffa325d54e64544c9769d7e4a.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the period is $\\pi .$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the graph of the function passes through the point $(0,0).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{5\\pi }{6}).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84e0a734-5caa-53e6-95cb-8ebb089583f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295980} {:answer/id #uuid "b1dbaf5a-ef2e-5a0c-af17-283db49b71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296204} {:answer/id #uuid "e7f54506-f8f9-5e84-a336-30e0e1061dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296499} {:answer/id #uuid "eaf5e982-270e-5ac6-907b-4a07fbb8da8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296515} {:answer/id #uuid "ed52198b-4523-5c6a-85f8-e3abbb92970e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1dbaf5a-ef2e-5a0c-af17-283db49b71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296204} :answer-field/id #uuid "59ae0b34-6270-5c87-9457-d86beb87e7e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296816}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4be11add-d875-5219-b83f-33d16bf37abb" :question/math-academy-id "q-28675" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=tan⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\n- $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).$\n- The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi $\n- $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/31/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+\\pi )=tan⁡(x)=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$\n\n- Statement II is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2})=tan⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi )=tan⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064a647e-d06a-50bb-9cbc-0f17389eca42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295298} {:answer/id #uuid "1066d92d-62c9-5dad-8b4c-dbbe71386d05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295362} {:answer/id #uuid "3f3a0291-6ad9-5566-9fd5-0de08933b4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295630} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8ba8e5-5fce-5a75-b9a3-f9b2aab87da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296026} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2ff4e9-ee34-51e6-b267-06c09d19013f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e8ba8e5-5fce-5a75-b9a3-f9b2aab87da3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296026} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1618392-44be-533c-81a8-efd84eeee3ac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297006}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c5a3a079-0ec8-5b33-84d2-568517288149" :question/math-academy-id "q-29608" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nI. The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/31/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )=tan⁡(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}]}
